<title>USA: Northeast Indiana Bancorp to buy back shrs.</title>
<headline>Northeast Indiana Bancorp to buy back shrs.</headline>
<dateline>HUNTINGTON, Ind. 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northeast Indiana Bancorp Inc said Friday it planned to repurchase about 10 percent of its outstanding stock, or 176,273 shares, in the open market over the next 12 months.</p>
<p>&quot;We continue to be of the opinion that the repurchase of our shares represents an attractive investment opportunity which will benefit the company and our stockholders,&quot; the company's president, Stephen Zahn, said in a news release.</p>
<p>Northeast Indiana shares were down 1/4 at 16-1/4 early Friday afternoon.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
